@startuml Sequence_A_Failover
hide footbox
autonumber
actor User
participant "Bank Core" as Core
participant "Notification API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Outbox Relay" as Relay
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Temporal Starter" as Starter
participant "Temporal Workflow" as WF
participant "Push Activity" as Push
participant "FCM / APNs" as FCM
participant "Mobile App" as App
participant "Callback API" as Callback
participant "SMS Activity" as SMS
participant "SMS Provider" as SMSP

Core -> API: POST critical event + idempotency_key
API -> DB: Persist notification + inbox + outbox
DB --> API: COMMIT
API --> Core: 202 Accepted + notification_id
Relay -> Kafka: Publish transactional event
Kafka -> Starter: Consume
Starter -> WF: Start Workflow(notification_id)
WF -> Push: Send push
Push -> FCM: Submit push
FCM --> Push: Accepted (not device delivery)
Push -> DB: Store provider acceptance
WF -> WF: Wait for App ACK or durable 8s timer
... 8 seconds; no App ACK ...
WF -> DB: Reserve SMS attempt (idempotent state transition)
WF -> SMS: Send SMS(attempt_id, idempotency_key)
SMS -> SMSP: Submit SMS
SMSP --> SMS: Accepted + provider_message_id
SMS -> DB: Store SMS provider acceptance
SMSP -> User: Deliver SMS (carrier dependent)
SMSP -> Callback: Delivery receipt (if supported)
Callback -> WF: Signal SMS delivery status
WF -> DB: Append transition; mark delivered/unconfirmed
note over WF,App
If a late Push/App ACK arrives after SMS dispatch,
the platform records duplicate_risk. It cannot retract
an SMS already accepted by the provider.
end note
@enduml
